From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 21:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] dxvk: no shared handle for an image or fence the device
 cannot share

A D3D11 texture created with D3D11_RESOURCE_MISC_SHARED asks DxvkImage
for exportable memory. canShareImage refuses it on a device without
VK_KHR_external_memory_win32 (KosmicKrisp has none), so m_shared is false
and the image is allocated as an ordinary one; but allocateStorageWithUsage
still passed the sharing's handle type to the allocator, which then called
DxvkResourceAllocation::initKmtHandles, and that calls
vkGetMemoryWin32HandleKHR: a NULL function pointer on such a device.
Hollow Knight's Media Foundation video path (mfplat, winegstreamer) creates
such a texture on a thread-pool worker after New Game; the call through
NULL ended the game with 0xc0000005 on the D3D12 route and on DXVK with
tiler mode off. The allocation now carries the handle type only when the
image is shared.

DxvkFence had the same shape: it called initKmtHandles, and so
vkGetSemaphoreWin32HandleKHR, for any shared type, even when the device
reported the semaphore type as not exportable and created a plain one.
It now does so only for an exportable semaphore whose function loaded.

On a device with the extensions nothing changes.

Class: upstream-bug
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-06-vulkan-perf-baseline.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 src/dxvk/dxvk_fence.cpp | 7 ++++++-
 src/dxvk/dxvk_image.cpp | 7 ++++++-
 2 files changed, 12 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/dxvk/dxvk_fence.cpp b/src/dxvk/dxvk_fence.cpp
index 8485c40..87f8428 100644
--- a/src/dxvk/dxvk_fence.cpp
+++ b/src/dxvk/dxvk_fence.cpp
@@ -57,7 +57,12 @@ namespace dxvk {
       }
     }
 
-    if (info.sharedType != VK_EXTERNAL_SEMAPHORE_HANDLE_TYPE_FLAG_BITS_MAX_ENUM)
+    // Only an exportable semaphore has a handle to open: without
+    // VK_KHR_external_semaphore_win32 the call would go to a function
+    // the device never loaded.
+    if (info.sharedType != VK_EXTERNAL_SEMAPHORE_HANDLE_TYPE_FLAG_BITS_MAX_ENUM
+     && (externalFeatures & VK_EXTERNAL_SEMAPHORE_FEATURE_EXPORTABLE_BIT)
+     && m_vkd->vkGetSemaphoreWin32HandleKHR)
       initKmtHandles();
   }
 
diff --git a/src/dxvk/dxvk_image.cpp b/src/dxvk/dxvk_image.cpp
index 3b5b739..9111633 100644
--- a/src/dxvk/dxvk_image.cpp
+++ b/src/dxvk/dxvk_image.cpp
@@ -334,7 +334,12 @@ namespace dxvk {
     allocationInfo.resourceCookie = cookie();
     allocationInfo.properties = m_properties;
     allocationInfo.mode = mode;
-    allocationInfo.handleType = m_info.sharing.type;
+    // Only an image that can be shared has exportable memory: one whose sharing
+    // canShareImage refused (no VK_KHR_external_memory_win32) is an ordinary image,
+    // and asking for its handle would call a function the device never loaded.
+    allocationInfo.handleType = m_shared
+      ? m_info.sharing.type
+      : VK_EXTERNAL_MEMORY_HANDLE_TYPE_FLAG_BITS_MAX_ENUM;
 
     if (m_info.transient)
       allocationInfo.mode.set(DxvkAllocationMode::NoDedicated);
